VAL_TABLE_ MPPT_Fault 8 "Fault" 7 "Phase Over Current" 6 "Input Under Current" 5 "Input Over Current" 4 "Output Over Current" 3 "Output Over Voltage" 2 "Input Over Voltage" 1 "Configuration Error" 0 "OK(No Fault)" ;

CM_ "
Message ID:
    [board ID][   msg ID   ]
    [   4b   ][     7b     ]

Node IDs:

    4 most dominant bits (highest prio)
    ====================
    <source board> | <board ID>[bin] | <board ID>[dec] | <starting frame ID>[dec]
    RPI_TB         | 0000            | 0               | 0
    STEERING_WHEEL | 0001            | 1               | 128
    INS            | 0010            | 2               | 256
    LEFT_SERVO     | 0011            | 3               | 384
    RIGHT_SERVO    | 0100            | 4               | 512
    BACK_SERVO     | 0101            | 5               | 640
    HEIGHT_SENSOR  | 0110            | 6               | 768
    MOTOR          | 0111            | 7               | 896
    ESC            | 1000            | 8               | 1024
    BMS            | 1001            | 9               | 1152
    MPPT 1         | 1010            | 10              | 1280
    MPPT 2         | 1011            | 11              | 1408
    MPPT 3         | 1100            | 12              | 1536
    MPPT 4         | 1101            | 13              | 1664
    MPPT 5         | 1110            | 14              | 1792
    MPPT 6         | 1111            | 15              | 1920

================== ESC FRAMES NOTE =============================

Message ID calculation:
    Board ID 7 (MOTOR/ESC) uses binary 0111 in the 4 MSB of an 11-bit ID.
    Base Address = 0x380 (896 decimal) [cite: 72-73].

ESC Details (HBCi3 Protocol V15):
    Telemetry Packets 1-7 integrated [cite: 36-53].
    Baudrate: 125 kbps.
    Source Node: ESC.
================== REFACTOR NOTES ==============================

125 kbps = 125000 bps

SOF + ID + RTR + IDE + RB + DLC + DATA + CRC + CRCD + ACKS + ACKD + EOF + IFS
1 + 11 + 1 + 1 + 1 + 4 + 64 + 15 + 1 + 1 + 1 + 7 + 3 = 111
125000 / 111 = 1126 fps ~= 1000 fps (duzio)
dla 9 płytek górna granica 100 ramek / sekunde / płytke (100 Hz = 10 frames/milisecond)";
